sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R1-R4 (process.stop shape), ADR 0242 signed apt sources, single-swamp-node.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: tool:install
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  CLI->>GW: tool:install ripgrep<br/>--node=12 --manager=apt
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit tool:install ripgrep --node=12 --manager=apt`
  %%> - syntax: `<package> --node=ID --manager=MANAGER [--constraint=RANGE] [--repository=JSON]`
  %%> Input:
  %%> - the package, as its manager names it
  %%> - the Node and the Tool Manager: `apt`, `composer`, `vp`, `brew` or `brew-cask`, as the Node's platform supports
  %%> - optionally a SemVer constraint, which only stops an unsafe version
  %%> - optionally a signed apt repository, for packages outside Ubuntu's own (ADR 0242)
  Note over GW: Validate, lock the manager<br/>Tool: installing · task #5133
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - your Node has an access grant to Node 12
  %%> - Node 12's platform supports the Tool Manager, and its installation isn't conflicting
  %%> - the package isn't already a Tool on Node 12
  %%> - the package isn't protected: packages Orbit manages itself, such as Caddy or PHP, can't become Tools
  %%> - no other change runs for this Tool Manager on Node 12; the Gateway holds one lock per Node and Tool Manager
  %%> Result:
  %%> - Tool `ripgrep` recorded as installing (the record is dropped if the Tool Manager setup fails)
  %%> - task #5133 recorded with the full intent
  %%> - nothing has happened on the Node yet
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-tool-write
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run on serve (Node 209)
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the package, manager, constraint and repository definition
  %%> - Node 12's address and SSH host keys; the SSH identity comes from the `swamp` role
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5133
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task number, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  opt Tool Manager not ready yet
    SW->>N: Set up the Tool Manager<br/>Linux first use · pinned version
    %%> When:
    %%> - only on Linux, the first time this Tool Manager is used on the Node
    %%> Per Tool Manager:
    %%> - `apt`: always ready; `node:add` sets it up
    %%> - `composer`: installed on first use (or with the `app-dev`/`app-prod` role)
    %%> - `vp` (Vite+): installed on first use (or with an application role)
    %%> - `brew` (Homebrew): installs a pinned Homebrew revision on first use
    %%> - macOS (`brew`, `brew-cask`, `vp`): never installed by Orbit; Orbit only checks the existing installation
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - installs the Tool Manager itself at a pinned version and checks that version
    %%> Not supported:
    %%> - other Tool Managers such as `mise`; Orbit has five, fixed in code
  end
  opt --repository given
    SW->>N: Add the signed apt source<br/>key checked by fingerprint
    %%> When:
    %%> - only for `apt` with `--repository`
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - downloads the signing key and checks its fingerprint
    %%> - adds the apt source, so apt trusts only packages signed with that key
  end
  SW->>N: Check the candidate<br/>version vs constraint
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks the manager which version it would install
  %%> - compares it with the constraint; a version outside it stops the run here
  SW->>N: Install the package<br/>apt-get install --no-remove
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - installs the package with the manager
  %%> - for `apt`, never removes other packages to make room
  %%> Busy apt lock:
  %%> - when Ubuntu's automatic updates hold the apt lock, it waits for the lock within the run's time budget, then fails
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - root for `apt`; the Node's managed user for `composer` and `vp`
  alt install succeeds
    N-->>SW: ripgrep 14.1.0 installed
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the installed version, read back from the manager
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>Tool: installed 14.1.0
    %%> Result:
    %%> - Tool `ripgrep` recorded as installed, version 14.1.0
    %%> - the apt repository recorded, when one was given
    %%> - task #5133 succeeds
  else a step fails
    N--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or no candidate
    %%> When:
    %%> - the manager can't install, the key doesn't match, or no version fits the constraint
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Mark what failed<br/>Tool Manager or Tool · rerun
    %%> Result when the Tool Manager setup failed:
    %%> - the Tool Manager is marked failed
    %%> - no Tool is recorded
    %%> Result when the install failed:
    %%> - Tool `ripgrep` marked failed, so you can see it
    %%> Always:
    %%> - task #5133 fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - a manager or apt source set up before the failure stays; a rerun reuses it
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5133
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
